-- Data for the student beta test plan (Documentation/RevisionHub_Student_Beta_Test_Plan.xlsx).
-- Run it after the migrations (it needs Tests.isActive from 20261103-test-archive.sql):
--
--   docker compose exec -T db sh -c \
--       'mariadb -u"$MARIADB_USER" -p"$MARIADB_PASSWORD" "$MARIADB_DATABASE"' \
--       < database/seeds/beta-test-data.sql
--
-- It uses fixed IDs and INSERT IGNORE, so running it again adds nothing twice. Dates are worked
-- out from the day it is run, so due dates and the results chart stay current. Do not run it on
-- a live server, every account has the known password below. Generated, edit the generator
-- rather than this file by hand if it needs to change a lot.
--
-- Every account's password: Revision1!
--
-- Give each tester their own set (N = 1, 2 or 3), so locking an account or taking tests
-- doesn't get in the way of another tester:
--   ws900001  main account for beta tester 1 (Beta Testing Cohort, 7 completed tests, 820 points)
--   ws900002  main account for beta tester 2 (Beta Testing Cohort, 7 completed tests, 820 points)
--   ws900003  main account for beta tester 3 (Beta Testing Cohort, 7 completed tests, 820 points)
--   ws90001N  approved, never taken a test (SEL-07, RES-05). Beta New Starters cohort, where nobody
--             has points yet (LB-08)
--   ws90002N  registered but email not verified (VER-12)
--   ws90003N  email verified, waiting for lecturer approval (VER-13)
--
-- Shared:
--   ws900040  has an expired verification link (VER-05). Don't log in as it, a resend replaces
--             the link; running this file again puts the expired link back. The link is:
--             http://localhost:5173/verify-email?token=8c3d301a43f58313388635a21ac7c3404d0a7d0b0306908c95a2afc0a58dfc87
--   ws800001  Alex Brown, already registered: use alex.brown@example.com / ws800001 for the
--             duplicate email and student number tests (REG-14, REG-15)
--   hcarter, treid  lecturers who set the tests
--
-- What the main tester accounts see:
--   Tests page   7 tests, soonest due first and no-due-date last (SEL-03):
--                Normalisation Quiz (due 5 days ago, SEL-04), SQL Fundamentals (10 min, due in
--                3 days), HTML & CSS Basics (15 min, 10 drawn from a pool of 20, TST-05),
--                JavaScript Essentials (untimed, TST-09, full marks already, SEL-08 / TST-15),
--                Cyber Security Intro, Quick Fire Networking (1 minute, TST-08), Study Skills
--                Warm-up (3 easy questions, full marks possible, TST-14)
--   Completed    7 attempts, so 2 pages (SEL-06), spread from 10 days to 14 months ago (RES-04),
--                some with unanswered questions
--   Leaderboard  Alex B. 1st, Priya P. 2nd, the three testers tied 3rd (LB-01 to LB-06).
--                Jordan K. tops Networking, nobody has points in Cyber Security (LB-05, LB-08)
--   Hidden       Marketing Basics belongs to Beta Other Cohort (SEL-09): /testing/be7a0004-0000-4000-8000-000000000008
--                Alex Brown's attempt (ANS-02): /testing/answers/be7a0008-0000-4000-8000-000000000022
--                Beta Closed Cohort is disabled, so it isn't in the registration cohort list
--
-- Registration tests use ws123456 and ws123457, so nothing here uses those student numbers.

START TRANSACTION;

